" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
" Plugin manager — vim-plug
" ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
" Not managed here — installed directly per machine, same convention as
" Oh My Zsh in zsh_setup.md:
"   curl -fLo ~/.vim/autoload/plug.vim --create-dirs \
"     https://raw.githubusercontent.com/junegunn/vim-plug/master/plug.vim
call plug#begin('~/.vim/plugged')

" Markdown live preview — opens in the default browser, auto-refreshes
" on save. previm runs its own local preview server using whichever of
" python/ruby/php it finds (python3 here, no Node/npm needed).
Plug 'tyru/open-browser.vim'
Plug 'kannokanno/previm'

call plug#end()

" previm shells out to open-browser.vim, whose default already picks
" the right opener (xdg-open on Linux, open on macOS) — no g:previm_open_cmd
" override needed, so this works unmodified on geekom-linux, mba13-linux,
" mba13-mac, and mbp16-mac alike.

" Markdown preview: ':PrevimOpen' while editing a .md file.
